      "writtenOn": "2021-04-05T07:13:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This has the (benign) side-effect of selecting upstream twice for each default network change : once when the broadcast is received, once when the link properties callback is received.\n\nISTM that with this change, we can simply stop listening to CONNECTIVITY_ACTION in Tethering.java, since eventually all it does is send CMD_UPSTREAM_CHANGED, which should have the same effect as this. Then you can add b/120533402 to the list of bugs fixed by this.",
      "revId": "2048b262458f8030712b626a4ce8dfe6fb9cb379",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8bb0a064_31452d0a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-05T13:03:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that might break DUN, which doesn\u0027t use mDefaultInternetNetwork like we do here. Also I don\u0027t know what would happen to legacy-type-based upstream selection. I think that might break as well.",
      "parentUuid": "7aa6946c_3938e098",
      "revId": "2048b262458f8030712b626a4ce8dfe6fb9cb379",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "deee2287_06ced51d",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java",
