        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-05T07:13:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of adding this new code path, should we simply add EVENT_DEFAULT_SWITCHED to EVENT_UPSTREAM_PERMISSION_CHANGED and CMD_UPSTREAM_CHANGED in l.1876 ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1721,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1726,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "2048b262458f8030712b626a4ce8dfe6fb9cb379",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf12851e_17bc29fe",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1726,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-05T13:03:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EVENT_UPSTREAM_PERMISSION_CHANGED and CMD_UPSTREAM_CHANGED are not comparable to EVENT_DEFAULT_SWITCHED. The first two are messages understood by TetherMainSM; the third is a \"subtype\" of EVENT_UPSTREAM_CALLBACK (which multiplexes different types of messages using arg1). Yes, this is confusing; unfortunately a lot of this code is.\n\nAs for reusing the code, there\u0027s another issue: line 1876 sets mTryCell to false and I don\u0027t know the implications of that. I *think* it does not do anything, but given the state this code is in, I don\u0027t want to touch it any more than necessary until we have time to write more tests for it.\n\nLeft as is for now.",
      "parentUuid": "deee2287_06ced51d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1721,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1726,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "2048b262458f8030712b626a4ce8dfe6fb9cb379",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
